NAME
       uptime - show how long the system has been running and its load

SYNOPSIS
       uptime [-p] [-s]

DESCRIPTION
       uptime prints one line: the time now, how long the system has been up,
       how many users are logged in, and the load average for the last 1, 5
       and 15 minutes. The load average is the number of processes running
       or waiting to run, on average. A load higher than the number of CPUs
       (see nproc) for a long time means the system is overloaded.

OPTIONS
       -p, --pretty
              Print only the time up, in words.

       -s, --since
              Print when the system started.

EXAMPLES
           uptime
           uptime -s

SEE ALSO
       top(1), w(1), nproc(1)
